From 4def766d417c6d915553b1a1837d731daadc8cb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:34:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(local-music): import a library from plain File objects

Android Chrome and iOS Safari have no showDirectoryPicker, and Android's WebView cannot
provide one either, so the whole local library was unreachable on phones. This adds a
handle-less import path alongside the existing directory-picker one.

- add src/services/localAudioBinaryStore.ts: OPFS-backed audio byte store under
  folia-cache/local-audio-assets, keyed by a self-describing id derived from the song
  record alone, so playback/cover/delete all rebuild the same key with no second index
- importLocalFiles(File[]) and importLocalFilesViaInput() on localMusicService
- FileEntryForImport.handle is now optional; metadata, sidecar lyrics and covers are
  parsed for handle-less entries too
- getAudioFromLocalSong / getFileFromLocalSong / getLocalSongArrayBuffer fall back to
  the stored bytes when no handle is reachable
- resyncFolder / resyncAllFolders no-op for roots that have no directory handle
- getLocalFileImportAvailability() plus resolveLocalHomeAvailability() so the local tab
  is reachable when only the file input is available
